{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
BSD cubed provides experimental GNOME47 Wayland integration.
It is not a complete logind replacement or a hardware-readiness guarantee.

Use 'bsddd --probe' as an ordinary user to inspect ConsoleKit sessions.
The rc.d service is disabled by default; the bus policy permits only root
to own login1. It does not replace an existing owner.
Power and inhibit stay denied unless the caller is a non-root member of
bsddd_power_group (default operator) in an active local ConsoleKit session
and PolicyKit authorizes that caller's bus name. Uid 0 is never accepted.
The ordinary-user bsd3-session launcher requires a real controlling VT.
An opt-in SDDM example is in share/examples/bsd-cubed/sddm-wayland.conf.
Installation does not activate it or modify PAM. Test in a disposable VM
and an isolated boot environment before hardware integration.
EOM
}
